+# Static IPFS Deployment
+
+These commands build the site as static files for IPFS. They do not run during local development, and this repo does not upload anything automatically.
+
+## 1. Deploy the Contract on Base
+
+Use a real Base deployer only when you are ready for production USDC tips:
+
+```bash
+yarn deploy --file DeployUsdcTipJar.s.sol --network base --keystore <foundry-keystore-name>
+```
+
+This updates `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` with the Base chain ID `8453` deployment.
+
+## 2. Build the Static Site
+
+Set a stable production origin before building. Use a domain, IPNS name, or ENS gateway URL that will serve the IPFS release.
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+rm -rf .next out
+
+NEXT_PUBLIC_TARGET_NETWORK=base \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://<production-origin>" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL="https://mainnet.base.org" \
+yarn build
+```
+
+If your build host is Node 25 and static prerendering fails inside wallet storage code, retry with a Node runtime from the project range in `package.json` or run the build with a Node-supported localStorage backing-file flag.
+
+Pre-upload checks:
+
+```bash
+test -f out/index.html
+test -f out/debug/index.html
+ls out/*/index.html
+grep -R "https://<production-origin>" out | head
+```
+
+## 3. Upload to IPFS
+
+Using the project dependency `bgipfs`:
+
+```bash
+CID=$(yarn bgipfs upload out | tee /tmp/usdc-tipjar-ipfs-upload.log | grep -o 'CID: [^ ]*' | awk '{print $2}')
+test -n "$CID"
+echo "CID=$CID"
+```
+
+## 4. Verify the Uploaded Site
+
+Replace `<gateway>` with the gateway you use for review.
+
+```bash
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://<gateway>/ipfs/$CID/"
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://<gateway>/ipfs/$CID/debug/"
+curl -sL "https://<gateway>/ipfs/$CID/" | grep "Base USDC Tip Jar"
+curl -sL "https://<gateway>/ipfs/$CID/" | grep "https://<production-origin>"
+```
+
+Expected results:
+
+```text
+200
+200
+```
+
+Review the gateway URL in a browser, connect a wallet on Base, and send a small production tip only after the contract address and recipient are confirmed.
